 "_doc": "nektos/act's OWN test corpus for pkg/workflowpattern, extracted verbatim from workflow_pattern_test.go @ 4f411281417e88660bea1c1a1749aa71ae0bd60f (MIT). Unlike gha-filter-oracle.json (single pattern/value pairs from GitHub's published cheat sheet) this corpus exercises the SET logic \u2014 how a LIST of patterns, including negated ones, combines over a LIST of inputs. That combination is where order-sensitive '!' re-includes live, and it is not testable one pair at a time. skip  = the include-list semantics (branches:, tags:, paths:)  -> true means the workflow is SKIPPED. filter = the ignore-list semantics (branches-ignore:, paths-ignore:) -> true means SKIPPED. Contributed by ship 002's rebuild (2026-08-03). Extend, never trim.",
